### 3. Compound interest and compounding returns

Returns earned on money that has already earned returns.

For example, $100,000 growing at a hypothetical 7% annually becomes about $196,700 after 10 years without additional contributions.

Why it matters: Starting early, investing consistently, and avoiding unnecessary withdrawals can make time one of your most valuable financial assets. Actual market returns are variable and not guaranteed.

