### 4. Profit versus revenue

- Revenue: What your business earns before expenses.
- Gross profit: Revenue minus the direct cost of delivering your products or services.
- Net profit: What remains after the relevant expenses.
- Cash flow: When money actually enters and leaves your accounts.

Why it matters: A web development or engineering business can look profitable on paper while struggling to pay bills because clients pay late or projects consume too many hours.

