### 7. Interest rates and cost of debt

- APR: Annual percentage rate, which helps express the yearly cost of borrowing, including certain fees.
- Amortization: How loan payments are allocated to interest and principal over time.
- Debt-to-income ratio (DTI): Monthly debt payments divided by gross monthly income.

Why it matters: High-interest consumer debt can undermine wealth-building. A mortgage, business loan, and credit card balance should not automatically be treated as equivalent kinds of debt.

