### 11. Retirement accounts and financial independence

Learn the differences among a 401(k), traditional IRA, Roth IRA, and self-employed retirement plans such as a SEP IRA or solo 401(k), where eligible.

Financial independence means having sufficient assets or reliable income to cover your living expenses without depending entirely on active employment.

Why it matters: Your business can fund your wealth-building plan, but you don't want your entire future tied to the business succeeding indefinitely.

