### 12. Estate planning and generational wealth

- Will: Specifies how your property should be handled and can nominate guardians for minor children, subject to applicable law.
- Trust: A legal arrangement for holding and managing assets under defined terms.
- Beneficiary designation: Identifies who receives eligible account or policy proceeds.
- Estate tax: A tax that may apply to an estate under applicable rules.

Why it matters: Building wealth for a large family includes deciding who manages assets, who receives them, and how dependents are cared for if something happens to you.

## 2. The business finance terms that could make you wealthy

Your technical background gives you an advantage here. You can understand systems, automate processes, and create things that solve repeatable problems. The challenge is learning to think like an owner of assets rather than only a provider of services.

These are the terms I'd prioritize for your situation.

| Term | What it means | How to use it |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Billable rate | What you charge per hour of work | Price projects to account for overhead, taxes, and profit. |
| Utilization rate | The percentage of available work time spent on billable work | Understand why a high hourly rate doesn't always produce high income. |
| Customer acquisition cost (CAC) | How much it costs to acquire a customer | Find profitable ways to attract clients. |
| Customer lifetime value (LTV) | The gross profit or contribution a customer generates over the relationship | Decide how much to invest in acquiring and retaining customers. |
| Recurring revenue | Revenue that repeats on a predictable schedule | Build maintenance contracts, hosting services, subscriptions, or ongoing engineering support. |
| Gross margin | Revenue remaining after direct delivery costs, expressed as a percentage | Identify your most profitable services. |
| Operating margin | Operating profit divided by revenue | Measure how efficiently the business operates. |
| Accounts receivable (AR) | Money customers owe your business | Reduce late payments and improve cash flow. |
| Working capital | Current assets minus current liabilities | Ensure the business can meet its short-term obligations. |
| Customer concentration | How dependent your business is on a few clients | Avoid letting one client's departure threaten your family's finances. |
| Intellectual property (IP) | Valuable creations such as code, designs, processes, and patents | Build reusable products and establish clear ownership rights. |
| Business valuation | An estimate of what the business is worth | Build something that could eventually be sold, transferred, or operated without you. |

